[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      98[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Documented UB (rows 36, 37, 46) — why these are not asserted
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      99[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     100[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Three inputs make the **C** read memory it never wrote, so the C has no defined
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     101[0m:[38;5;10m[49m result to match:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     102[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     103[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Row 36** — `typeA`/`typeB` outside `{0,1,2}`: `c2MakeProxy`'s `switch` has no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     104[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `default:`, so inside `c2GJK` the local `c2Proxy pA;` stays uninitialised and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     105[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `pA.count` / `pA.verts[0]` are read as stack garbage. The *defined* half of the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     106[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   same behaviour — a direct `c2MakeProxy` call, where the caller owns the proxy —
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     107[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   **is** asserted (row 1), including `0xFFFFFFFF` and a NULL `shape`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     108[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Row 37** — `cache->count > 3`: reads `cache->iA[i]` past `iA[3]`, writes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     109[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `saveA[i]` past `saveA[3]`, and writes `verts[i]` past the 4 `c2sv` slots of
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     110[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `c2Simplex`. The result depends on the compiler's stack frame layout.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     111[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Row 46** — a cache index at or beyond the proxy's vertex count.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     112[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     113[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The Rust zero-initialises `c2Proxy` and `c2Simplex` (`::default()`), so on these
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     114[0m:[38;5;10m[49m paths the Rust is **deterministic where the C is not**. This is a deliberate,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     115[0m:[38;5;10m[49m documented deviation confined to UB-only inputs: no choice of Rust code can
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     116[0m:[38;5;10m[49m reproduce GCC's stack garbage, and zero-init is the memory-safe option. All
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     117[0m:[38;5;10m[49m *defined* neighbours of these boundaries (cache `count` 0, 1, 2, 3 and negative;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     118[0m:[38;5;10m[49m every in-range `iA`/`iB` combination) are asserted.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     119[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     120[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Mutation evidence
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     121[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     122[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `scripts/mutation_battery.sh` injects 55 known-wrong changes into
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     123[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `src/lib.rs` — every numeric constant, every comparison operator, every
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     124[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `switch`-arm body and vertex shuffle — rebuilds the cdylib and re-runs the whole
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     125[0m:[38;5;10m[49m suite. Result: **46 killed, 9 survivors, and every survivor is provably an
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     126[0m:[38;5;10m[49m equivalent mutant**:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     127[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     128[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | surviving mutant | why it cannot be observed |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     129[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|---|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     130[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `while (iter < 20)` → `< 19`, → `< 8` | The maximum reachable `iter` is **7**, measured over 60M randomized calls. Proxies hold at most 4 vertices and the duplicate-support test ends the loop first, so the cap is dead. Lowering it to `< 7` (the reachable max) **is** killed, which proves the loop-cap mechanism itself is under test. |
