[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     113[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Adversarial reinforcement (`tests/phase_bc_adversarial.rs`)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     114[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     115[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Randomised floating-point inputs approach the C's strict `>` / `<=` boundaries
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     116[0m:[38;5;10m[49m but rarely land exactly on them. These sweeps use small integers, half-integers
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     117[0m:[38;5;10m[49m and exact powers of two so the arithmetic is exact and the boundaries are
